out.push(S('Stage 7R · Share'));
out.push(A('⚠ **Two counts on the board.** **How many covering lines contained _you may attach_?** **Three of ten.** **How many attachable paragraphs contained something about the writer\'s feelings?** **Seven, and all seven were unattachable for that reason alone** — **so read one aloud, strike the sentence in front of the room, and read it again.** **Then Mr Tayara\'s four days and the three words in the margin.**'));

// ===================== 18.3 =====================
out.push(pb());
out.push(h2('18.3  What the rule is for'));
out.push(S('Stage 1 · Get ready'));
out.push(A('**a** Open. ⚠ **What it is for, not what it does.** **Nine of ten give what the rule does** — _it stops people registering twice_, _it keeps the deadline fair_ — **and the repair is one question: why is that worth doing?** **Strike every sentence that begins _it stops people from_ without an answer to that, and the board will be nearly empty, which is the right starting point.**'));
out.push(A('**b** Argue from the purpose: **2** and **4**. ⚠ **2 states the purpose and shows it already met, on the body\'s own list.** **4 states the purpose and shows that no other scheme used a later set of figures.** **1, 3 and 5 are unfairness, an appeal for a child and a claim about intention** — **and the third is the most seductive, because an applicant cannot know what anybody intended and a clerk cannot act on it.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 2 · Listen and read'));
out.push(A('**a** **B** — ⚠ **the rule\'s own purpose**, with the case measured against it.'));
out.push(A('**b** **1** ⚠ **It is an argument to a person, and the person reading your letter is not permitted to be one** — **and a letter that asks them to be a person has asked for the one thing they cannot give and has offered no ground for the thing they can.**   **2** ⚠ **Derive it, state it as a derivation, and invite correction in the same sentence** — **because the reader either lets it stand, in which case your case is measured against it, or corrects it, and a correction is a written statement of purpose.**'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **This is the cycle in which a teacher is most likely to be contradicted by a student\'s own experience, and the contradiction must be taken seriously.** **Somebody will say that hardship worked for them.** **It does sometimes, with a particular person, once** — **and the honest answer is that it worked because of who was reading, that it is not available twice, and that it cannot be written down and taught.** **This unit teaches what works on a reader you cannot choose.** ⚠ **The derivation with its invitation is the architecture of the cycle and the room will think it weak.** **Put the arithmetic to them: four students in this class wrote the derivation and two had it corrected, and both corrections came back with a circular number attached** — **which is a document that did not exist until somebody stated a purpose and got it wrong in writing.**'));
out.push(S('Language box · Practise'));
out.push(A('**1** **A certificate against double registration** — _so that no pupil is registered at two schools in one year_ · **and the register shows no second registration.**   **2** **A deadline for a single set of figures** — _so that the round is scored against one set_ · **and no other scheme used a later set.**   **3** ⚠ **A definition protecting a count** — _so that two branches cannot report the same stock_ · **and the branch is the only one in the district.**   **4** **A purpose you must derive** — **state it, invite correction, and promise to write again on whatever purpose is given.**   **5** ⚠ **A case whose purpose is not met** — **say so and write nothing**, **which is what two students in this class did after two months of preparation.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 3 · Practise (sample – Card A)'));
out.push(SAMPLE([
  '**Row 1** **Purpose: so that no pupil is registered at two schools in one year.** ⚠ **Met: the governorate register shows no other registration.**',
  '**Row 2** ⚠ **Hardship.** **A clerk can refuse it kindly and will.** **Ask for the purpose instead.**',
  '**Row 3** **Purpose: so that a branch\'s stock can be identified against a record that cannot be altered.** ⚠ **Probably met: the day-book is in one hand, dated daily, and the governorate holds the only other copy.**',
  '**Row 4** ⚠ **A claim about intention** — **which the applicant cannot know and the clerk cannot act on.**',
  '**Row 5** **Purpose: so that experience is continuous rather than assembled.** ⚠ **Probably met at fourteen and ten months with a two-week gap** — **and the letter must give the gap, because the purpose turns on it.**',
]));
out.push(S('Stage 3 · Practise (sample – Card B)'));
out.push(SAMPLE([
  '**Row 1** **Purpose: so that the round is scored against a single set of figures.** ⚠ **Met: the figures were published by the governorate on the second and no other scheme used a later set.**',
  '**Row 2** ⚠ **Unfairness.** **Not a purpose, not a measurement, and the word _unfair_ puts the body in the wrong before any document is read.**',
  '**Row 3** **Purpose: so that a certificate can be traced to a body that can be asked about it.** ⚠ **Not met in the obvious way: the body closed in 2017, so nobody can be asked** — **and the honest letter says that the purpose cannot be met by anybody and asks what the body does in such cases, which is 18.4.**',
  '**Row 4** ⚠ **A flourish.** **_Sympathetic consideration_ names the power that does not exist.**',
  '**Row 5** **The hardest, and the purpose is not met.** ⚠ **A requirement that a degree be from a recognised institution exists so that the body can rely on an assessment it has not made itself** — **and a degree recognised in three countries and not here does not meet that purpose, because none of the three is the body.** **There is no exception to ask for and the honest route is 18.6.**',
]));
out.push(S('Stage 3R · Perform – listener task'));
out.push(A('**Rows 2 and 4 on both cards are hardship and the room says what a clerk can do with each, which is refuse it kindly.** ⚠ **Rows 5 are the pair the cycle turns on**: on Card A the purpose is probably met and on Card B it is not — **and the room must reach the second answer and say that there is no exception to ask for.** **Nobody enjoys that minute and it is the most useful one in the lesson.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 4 · Your turn (sample)'));
out.push(SAMPLE([
  '**The rule: form ED/2 requires a transfer certificate from the previous school.**',
  '**The purpose, derived.** _The certificate appears to exist in order that no pupil is registered at two schools in the same year; if that is not its purpose, I should be glad to be corrected and I shall write again on whatever purpose the directorate states._',
  '**The case measured against it.** **The governorate register shows no registration for file 4471 at any school in the governorate, and the only entry is an admission in 2019 at a school on the directorate\'s own closure list.**',
  '**b** ⚠ **My partner says it is a purpose and not a description, because it gives a reason for the requirement and not an effect of it.** **And my case meets it** — **and two in this room do not, and both of those two have been preparing to argue for two months.**',
]));
out.push(S('Stage 4R · Report (sample)'));
out.push(SAMPLE(['Mr Tayara wants an exception to the transfer certificate rule, and his first letter was about the boy: nine, two years out of school, nobody\'s fault, and it was refused in three lines, and the three lines were right, because he had asked a clerk to weigh a child against a regulation and she has no instrument for that. Mrs Oueidat said that is the thing to say first and plainly: hardship is not an argument to a system, it is an argument to a person, and the person reading your letter is not permitted to be one. Mrs Khoury said so the argument is the purpose, and what the certificate is for, in one sentence: so that no pupil is registered at two schools in one year. And then the case against the purpose: file 4471 cannot be registered twice, because the governorate\'s own list shows no other registration, which is not a request for discretion but a demonstration that the purpose is already met. Mr Attar asked where he got the purpose, since the circulars do not give one, and Mrs Khoury said you derive it, state it as a derivation, and invite correction in the same sentence. Dr Qabbani asked whether that does not weaken it, and Mrs Oueidat said it is the strongest form available: a stated purpose that invites correction cannot be dismissed, because the clerk either lets it stand, in which case the case is measured against it, or corrects it, and a correction is a written statement of purpose. Mrs Rizk said so either way you get the purpose, and Mrs Khoury said either way, and that is the whole architecture of the cycle: four students wrote the derivation, two had it corrected, and both corrections were more useful than the derivation. Mr Shihabi asked what happens if the purpose is met and the rule still bites, and then you have found an anomaly rather than a hardship and you say so in the system\'s own word, because an anomaly is a fault in a rule and a hardship is a fault in the world. Mrs Tarabishi asked what happens if the purpose is not met, and then you do not have an exception and you should not ask for one. Mrs Ajouz asked whether he still mentions the boy, and once, in a clause, as a fact and not as an argument. And Mr Tayara said the thing he will take away is the three lines that refused him, which are a good document: every word is true, and nothing in his letter had given her anything to put in a fourth line.']));
out.push(A('⚠ **The last line is the one to read twice and not explain.** **Mr Tayara still has the three lines that refused him and he calls them a good document: they say that the certificate is a requirement, that the directorate has no power to waive it, and that the file will be considered on resubmission.** **Every word is true** — **and nothing in his letter had given her anything to put in a fourth line.**'));
out.push(S('Board clinic – typical mistakes'));
out.push(A('**1** ⚠ **What the rule does, not what it is for** → **nine of ten.**   **2** **Hardship** → **an argument to a person, and the reader is not permitted to be one.**   **3** ⚠ _Nobody intended this_ → **a claim the applicant cannot know and the clerk cannot act on.**   **4** **A purpose asserted with no invitation to correct it** → **it can be dismissed in a line.**   **5** ⚠ _Anomalous_ **used for a hardship** → **an anomaly is a fault in a rule; a hardship is a fault in the world.**   **6** **A letter written where the purpose is not met** → **two of ten, and both had prepared for two months.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 5 · Read'));
out.push(A('**1** ⚠ **It is not a request for discretion.** **It asks whether a requirement applies to a case in which its purpose is already met** — **and it says in the same breath that it rests entirely on records the directorate holds, which is the sentence that makes the first claim checkable.**'));
out.push(A('**2** ⚠ **It states the purpose as a derivation and undertakes to write again on whatever purpose the directorate states.** **An ordinary request asserts a purpose or none** — **and this version cannot be dismissed, because the reader must either let it stand, in which case the case is measured against it, or correct it, which is a written statement of purpose the applicant could not otherwise obtain.**'));
out.push(A('**3** ⚠ **That if the purpose is other than he has stated, the letter falls** — **and that if the question cannot be determined at section level he will write wherever he is told rather than above anybody\'s head.** **The second is the sentence that distinguishes the letter from a threat, and it is the hinge of 18.4.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 6 · Write with help (sample)'));
out.push(SAMPLE([
  '**M. TAYARA** · _to the registration section_ · _file ED/2-4471_ · **19 April**',
  '**1 · What this letter is.** **It is not a request for discretion.** ⚠ **It asks whether a requirement applies to a case in which its purpose is already met.**',
  '**2 · The requirement.** **Form ED/2 requires a transfer certificate from the previous school.** **File 4471 is a pupil of nine for whom no previous school is on record.**',
  '**3 · The purpose, as I understand it.** ⚠ **The certificate appears to exist in order that no pupil is registered at two schools in the same year.** **If that is not its purpose, I should be glad to be corrected.**',
]));
out.push(S('Stage 7 · Write freely (sample, 284 words)'));
out.push(SAMPLE([
  '**H. RIZK** · _to the scheme secretariat_ · _scheme 7, spring round_ · **12 April**',
  '**1 · What this letter is.** **It is not a request for an extension and not an appeal against the closing date.** ⚠ **It asks whether the closing date applies to a submission whose only late element is a figure published by the governorate after the date.**',
  '**2 · The requirement.** **The scheme rules provide that applications close on 1 March.** **Scheme 7 was lodged on 26 February.** **The cost-per-household figure in annexe B is dated 2 March, because the governorate published its population figures on that day.**',
  '**3 · The purpose, as I understand it.** ⚠ **The closing date appears to exist in order that every scheme in a round is scored against a single set of figures.** **If that is not its purpose, I should be glad to be corrected, and I shall write again on whatever purpose the secretariat states.**',
  '**4 · The case measured against the purpose.** **The governorate published one set of figures, on 2 March, and every scheme in this round that gives a cost per household uses that set.** ⚠ **The secretariat\'s own scoring sheet for the round shows the same publication date against four of the nine schemes.** **Scoring against a single set is therefore not merely possible but unavoidable.**',
  '**5 · What follows, in the scheme\'s own terms.** **The requirement appears to be anomalous as applied to a figure the scheme itself could not have held before the closing date.** ⚠ **I am not asking for the date to be waived.** **I am asking whether it applies to annexe B.**',
  '**6 · What I can supply.** **The governorate\'s publication notice, the lodgement receipt of 26 February, and annexe B in its original form with the figure left blank.**',
  '**7 · What I accept.** **If the date applies to every page of a submission without exception, this letter falls and scheme 7 is late.**',
]));
out.push(S('Stage 7P · Respond (sample slip — band 3, with the answer)'));
out.push(SAMPLE([
  '**THE SLIP, unsigned.** **Reader: the secretariat.** **Absent: what the writer wants done with annexe B.** **Criterion — the line copied:** _"annexe B in its original form with the figure left blank"_. ⚠ **The letter offers two versions of annexe B and does not say which it asks the secretariat to score** — **and a secretariat that cannot tell will score the one that is complete and late.**',
  '**THE WRITER\'S ONE LINE.** ⚠ _Conceded: paragraph 6 now says that the version lodged on 26 February stands and that the figure may be added by the secretariat from the governorate\'s notice if it wishes._',
  '**A second slip, unsigned.** **Reader: the four other schemes using the same figures.** **Absent: that the letter cites them.**',
  '**THE WRITER\'S ONE LINE.** ⚠ _Refused: the four are cited from the secretariat\'s own scoring sheet and not from anything the schemes told me, and the citation is of a fact about the round rather than about them._',
]));
out.push(S('Stage 7R · Share'));
out.push(A('⚠ **Two numbers and one uncomfortable minute.** **Six cases of ten meet the purpose of their rule; two do not; two cannot be decided without a document nobody has.** **Then ask the two whose cases fail how long they had been preparing to argue** — **two months each, and neither will write the letter now.** **Say plainly that this is the cycle working.** **Then Mr Tayara\'s three lines, read flat.**'));

// ===================== 18.4 =====================
out.push(pb());
out.push(h2('18.4  The person who has to apply the rule'));
out.push(S('Stage 1 · Get ready'));
out.push(A('**a** Open. ⚠ **Their position, not their character.** **Eight of ten can name the post and two of the eight can say what it is permitted to decide** — **and the gap between those two numbers is the cycle.** **Write the ten posts on the board with a blank beside each and fill the blanks during the lesson, because seven of the ten powers are in a document the student already has.**'));
out.push(A('**b** Address the reader as somebody with a job: **2** and **4**. ⚠ **2 offers to be redirected and says it will write where it is sent.** **4 asks what they need and offers to supply it in any form they can use.** **1, 3 and 5 are a plea, an accusation of unwillingness and a threat** — **and 3 is the worst of the three, because _if you want to_ tells the reader that their refusal would be a choice.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 2 · Listen and read'));
out.push(A('**a** **B** — ⚠ **a sentence they can put in the file, and a question about what they need.**'));
out.push(A('**b** **1** ⚠ **It tells the reader that whatever they do, somebody senior will now read their file** — **so the safe course becomes a refusal in writing with the regulation quoted, and you will have a well-drafted refusal instead of a conversation.**   **2** ⚠ **Nothing is risked by a refusal and something is risked by a yes.** **A clerk who accepts a file gains nothing; a clerk who accepts it wrongly is the person who did** — **and a clerk who refuses forty files a week is never criticised for any of them.**'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **The arithmetic of the reader\'s position is the content of this cycle and it must go on the board as arithmetic.** **Nothing rewards a yes.** **A refusal costs the reader nothing and is never examined; an acceptance is the only thing anybody ever looks at.** **In 18.7\'s audio script a clerk says it in her own words: in twenty-six years nobody ever asked her why she had refused a file.** **Every move in this cycle follows from that** — **and a student who has not grasped it will write a letter asking for goodwill, which is a request for the one commodity the reader has no stock of.**'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **The question with nothing after it is the hardest instruction in the unit to obey and the easiest to check.** **_What would you need from me?_ and then stop.** **Nine of ten drafts in this class added a suggestion** — _perhaps a declaration, or a letter from the family_ — **and a suggestion must be refused before the real answer can be given, which costs a letter and about nine days.** **Make the room strike every clause after the question mark, out loud, in each other\'s drafts.** ⚠ **And teach the redirection sentence as the replacement for the threat, not as a politeness.** **A threat says that you will go above them; the redirection says that they may send you above them** — **and a reader who refers a file up has done their job, where a reader whose file is taken up has had it taken.**'));
out.push(S('Language box · Practise'));
out.push(A('**1** **A clerk who may attach** — _what would you need from me in order to attach a statement to field 7?_   **2** **A clerk who may only refer** — _if this is a question for the section head, I should be grateful to be told and I shall write there._   **3** ⚠ **A post you cannot identify** — **ask the body: _which office deals with a case in which no previous school is on record?_**   **4** **A refusal already received** — **the question becomes _what would have to be different?_**   **5** ⚠ **A case where the answer is to write elsewhere** — **and the letter thanks them for the redirection and does not argue with it.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 3 · Practise (sample – Card A)'));
out.push(SAMPLE([
  '**Row 1** **Powers: accept, return, refer.** **Sentence for the file: the attachable paragraph from 18.2.** ⚠ **Question: _what would you need from me in order to attach a statement to field 7?_**',
  '**Row 2** ⚠ **A threat.** **It produces a refusal in writing with the regulation quoted, which is almost impossible to reopen.**',
  '**Row 3** **Powers: determine whether a rule applies.** ⚠ **So the question is different: _is this a question your office determines, and if so what would you need?_**',
  '**Row 4** ⚠ **An accusation of unwillingness.** **_If you want to_ makes the refusal a choice and therefore a reproach.**',
  '**Row 5** **The hardest on the card.** ⚠ **Already refused in three lines** — **so the question is _what would have to be different for the file to be complete?_** **Not _why was it refused_, which invites the regulation again.**',
]));
out.push(S('Stage 3 · Practise (sample – Card B)'));
out.push(SAMPLE([
  '**Row 1** **Powers: accept a late form with a reason.** ⚠ **So the question is about the reason: _what form of reason does your office accept?_**',
  '**Row 2** ⚠ **Sympathy.** **It tells the reader you have formed a view of their working life, and they have forty files and no wish to be understood.**',
  '**Row 3** **Powers: put a case to the board.** ⚠ **Question: _what would the board need to see?_** **And nothing about the board\'s likely view, which is not yours to guess.**',
  '**Row 4** ⚠ **Sympathy with a figure of speech in it** — **_your hands are tied_ is a verdict on their office said in a friendly voice.**',
  '**Row 5** **A post you cannot identify.** ⚠ **The letter asks the body: _which office deals with a case of this kind?_** **One sentence, no case attached** — **because a case attached to that question gets a refusal from whoever opens the envelope.**',
]));
out.push(S('Stage 3R · Perform – listener task'));
out.push(A('**Rows 2 and 4 on both cards are threats or sympathy, and the room says what each produces**: a carefully drafted refusal, and a reader told that you have a view of their working life. ⚠ **Rows 5 are the hardest**: one has already refused you, so the question becomes _what would have to be different_, and one cannot be identified, **so the letter asks who deals with it.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 4 · Your turn (sample)'));
out.push(SAMPLE([
  '**The post: registration clerk, education directorate.**',
  '**Its powers, three.** **Accept a file.** **Return a file.** **Refer a question up.** ⚠ **I found all three in the directorate\'s own procedure note, which has been in my drawer since 2021.**',
  '**My question.** _What would you need from me in order to attach a statement to field 7?_',
  '**b** ⚠ **My partner struck the clause I had put after it, which was _a declaration, perhaps, or a letter from the family_.** **And the power I had been asking for in two months of letters was a fourth one** — **which is to decide that a regulation does not apply, and four of ten in this room found the same thing about themselves.**',
]));
out.push(S('Stage 4R · Report (sample)'));
out.push(SAMPLE(['Mr Tayara knows who reads form ED/2: a registration clerk, and the post is permitted to accept a file, return it, or refer it up. Three things, and he had spent two months writing to her as though she had a fourth, which was to decide that a regulation did not apply. Mrs Khoury asked what the fourth is worth to her, and nothing, and that is the sentence the room should take: if she accepts the file she gains nothing, if she accepts it wrongly she is the person who did, and a clerk who refuses forty files a week is never criticised for any of them. Mrs Oueidat asked what she can be given, and a sentence she can put in the file and a question: what would you need from me in order to attach a statement to field 7, and then nothing, because a suggestion is a thing she has to refuse before she can answer. Mr Attar asked whether she answered, and in six days, in two lines, asking for something he had not thought of: a declaration that no other registration is held, signed by him as head and not by the family, which took four minutes to write. Mrs Rizk asked about the threat, and Mrs Oueidat said it is the worst sentence available and the room will find it the most natural, because it tells a clerk that whatever she does somebody senior will now read her file, so the safe thing becomes the refusal in writing with the regulation quoted. Mrs Khoury said that is the mechanism worth saying twice: a threat does not make a clerk more likely to help, it makes the refusal more carefully written. Dr Qabbani asked about asking where it should go instead, and that is the opposite move and the one sentence that distinguishes a letter from a threat. Mr Shihabi asked whether it is not the same thing more politely, and Mrs Khoury said it is a different act and the difference is who chooses. Mrs Tarabishi asked about sympathy, and no, and this is the one place where kindness is a mistake. Mr Zahreddine asked whether the question is not a little passive, and Mrs Oueidat said it is the opposite, because a question with nothing after it obliges an answer, where a suggestion can be refused in one line and often is. And Mr Tayara said the thing he will take away is the six days and the four minutes: two months of letters about a regulation, and then one question about what she needed, answered in six days, and what she needed took him four minutes to write and nobody in two months of arguing had ever mentioned it.']));
out.push(A('⚠ **The last line is the finding and the two numbers in it are the whole argument: six days and four minutes.** **Two months of letters about a regulation, one question about what she needed, an answer in six days, and a declaration that took four minutes to write** — **and nobody in two months of arguing had ever mentioned it, because nobody had been asked.**'));
out.push(S('Board clinic – typical mistakes'));
out.push(A('**1** ⚠ **Asking for a power the post does not have** → **four of ten, and some had been doing it for months.**   **2** _I shall take it further_ → **a refusal, drafted to survive a section head.**   **3** ⚠ **A suggestion after the question** → **nine of ten; it must be refused before the answer can come.**   **4** **Sympathy for their position** → **a view of their working life they did not ask for.**   **5** ⚠ _If you want to_ → **the refusal becomes a choice and therefore a reproach.**   **6** **The file paragraph inside the letter** → **they cannot attach a page of your argument.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 5 · Read'));
out.push(A('**1** ⚠ **Nothing in the letter asks her to decide that a regulation does not apply.** **That is the fourth power, which the post does not have** — **and a reader who is asked for it drafts a refusal, because a refusal is the only safe document available to them.**'));
out.push(A('**2** ⚠ **It refuses to suggest what she might need or to propose any form of words beyond the attachable paragraph** — **and it offers instead to write the paragraph in whatever form her section uses, on the day he is told.** **A suggestion would have to be refused before she could answer; an offer to follow her form costs her nothing to accept.**'));
out.push(A('**3** ⚠ **So that she can attach it without attaching the letter.** **A clerk who must photocopy a page of somebody\'s argument to complete a file will not do it** — **and this is the sentence from the unit most likely to change a reader\'s working day, which is why it is in the model and not in a footnote.**'));
