out.push(S('Stage 7R · Share'));
out.push(A('⚠ **Two counts and one re-reading.** **How many borrowed clauses were heard as ironic?** **Six of ten, and four of the six had not intended it** — **so have those four read their clause again, flat, and let the room hear the difference.** **Then the four students who found no borrowable shape: three of their systems write plainly, which is worth four minutes.** **Then Mr Tayara\'s four words.**'));

// ===================== 18.6 =====================
out.push(pb());
out.push(h2('18.6  The institution with no category for you'));
out.push(S('Stage 1 · Get ready'));
out.push(A('**a** Open. ⚠ **Name them, and then name the nearest.** **Seven of ten can list the categories and three said their case fell outside all of them without having read the list** — **and the three are the cycle: all three turned out to meet most of the conditions of one category.** **Make the list the first thing on the board, in the schedule\'s own words.**'));
out.push(A('**b** Name the nearest and the single difference: **2** and **4**. ⚠ **2 names B, names one respect, and says what is the same.** **4 names category 2 and gives the single difference as an arithmetical fact.** **1, 3 and 5 are a refusal to be classified, a request for a new category and a claim to be beyond classification** — **and 3 is the expensive one, because it asks the reader to write a committee paper on behalf of one applicant.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 2 · Listen and read'));
out.push(A('**a** **B** — ⚠ **a new category** — and the letter must instead name the nearest and the single difference.'));
out.push(A('**b** **1** ⚠ **A fourth category**, **which is eighteen months and a committee paper written by the person he was writing to.**   **2** ⚠ **Never use it about yourself.** **It tells a body that nothing it has ever done can help you, which is a boast and a request for the committee at once** — **and it is wrong about four times in five, because almost nothing is unprecedented in an institution that is forty years old.**'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **The precedent question is the most productive single sentence in Book 2 and nobody in this class had ever asked it.** _I should be grateful to know whether a case of this kind has been determined before._ **Four students found a precedent within a week of asking, and one of the four found a case eleven years old that had gone into the category the writer had been told was closed to them.** **Teach it as arithmetic and not as cleverness**: a precedent is the safest document in any institution, so a body that has one will use it, and nobody goes looking for one on behalf of an applicant who has not asked whether one exists. ⚠ **And teach the second half of the sentence, which the room will drop.** **_And if the register holds no such case I shall say so in any further correspondence_** — **because it offers the body something in return, which is that the applicant will stop calling their case unusual.**'));
out.push(S('Language box · Practise'));
out.push(A('**1** **An awarding body not on a schedule** — _the nearest is B; the one difference is the institution, which was established after the list was last revised._   **2** **A registration in two parts** — _the nearest is category 2; the one difference is that mine is in two parts of fourteen and ten months._   **3** ⚠ **A right length and a wrong name** — **name the conditions met and count them before naming the difference.**   **4** **The precedent question** — **with its second half.**   **5** ⚠ **Two differences** — **two letters, or concede that you are asking for an exception and go to 18.3.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 3 · Practise (sample – Card A)'));
out.push(SAMPLE([
  '**Row 1** **Nearest: B.** **One difference: the awarding institution is not on the list, because it was established in 2014 after the list was last revised.** ⚠ **Precedent question, with its second half.**',
  '**Row 2** ⚠ **A request for a committee.** **Eighteen months, a paper written by your reader, on behalf of one applicant** — **and the honest answer is no.**',
  '**Row 3** **Nearest: the category whose content conditions you meet.** ⚠ **Count the conditions first: a name is one condition and content is usually five or six.**',
  '**Row 4** ⚠ **A claim to be beyond classification** — **which asks the reader to check every condition from the beginning and gives them no starting point.**',
  '**Row 5** **The hardest.** ⚠ **Two differences: the body and the length.** **Two letters, or concede the exception** — **and the room must choose out loud which difference it would give up, because a reader cannot tell and will refuse both.**',
]));
out.push(S('Stage 3 · Practise (sample – Card B)'));
out.push(SAMPLE([
  '**Row 1** **Nearest: category 2.** **One difference: fourteen and ten months against twenty-four continuous.** ⚠ **And the purpose of continuity is the 18.3 question hiding inside this cycle.**',
  '**Row 2** ⚠ _Unprecedented_ — **wrong four times in five, and a boast.**',
  '**Row 3** **Nearest: the category that names a certifying body.** ⚠ **One difference: the body closed in 2017** — **and the honest letter adds that no successor has been designated, which is a fact about the schedule.**',
  '**Row 4** ⚠ **_I do not fit_** — **which is a summary of ten conditions the reader must now check unaided.**',
  '**Row 5** **The honest one.** ⚠ **The nearest category is not the one the writer wants** — **and naming it anyway is the only honest reason in the unit for asking to be put in a category you would rather not be in.**',
]));
out.push(S('Stage 3R · Perform – listener task'));
out.push(A('**Rows 2 and 4 ask for a committee or claim to be beyond classification, and the room says what each costs the reader.** ⚠ **Rows 5 are the pair that matter**: one has two differences and must be split or conceded as an exception, **and one is the case where the nearest category is not the one the writer wants** — **the only honest reason for naming a category you would rather not be in.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 4 · Your turn (sample)'));
out.push(SAMPLE([
  '**The body: the syndicate\'s registration schedule, categories A, B and C.**',
  '**Nearest: B.** **Conditions met: nine of ten.**',
  '**The one difference.** **The awarding institution is not on the schedule\'s list, because it was established in 2014 and the list was last revised before then.**',
  '**The precedent question.** _I should be grateful to know whether a case of this kind has been determined before, and if the register holds no such case I shall say so in any further correspondence._',
  '**b** ⚠ **My partner says it is one difference and not two, because length and content are among the nine.** **And nobody in this room had asked the precedent question** — **and the syndicate had a case from 2016 which the secretary found in two days.**',
]));
out.push(S('Stage 4R · Report (sample)'));
out.push(SAMPLE(['Mr Attar has applied to a syndicate that has three categories and none of them is his: A, B and C, and he read the schedule properly for the first time in March, and his first letter asked for a fourth, which he now sees is the one request a register cannot grant, because a category is a line in a schedule and a schedule is amended by a committee that meets twice a year. Mrs Khoury asked what a fourth category costs them, and Mrs Oueidat said eighteen months and a committee paper, and the paper has to be written by the person you are writing to, so you have asked a secretary to put a proposal to a board about a schedule on behalf of one applicant. Mr Attar said he was refused in eleven lines and the last of them is the useful one: the schedule provides three categories and your qualification has not been considered under any of them, which told him what he had not seen, that nobody had looked at B, because he had not asked them to. Mrs Khoury said so the second letter names B, and names it and then names one difference, and the rest of the paragraph is what is the same. Dr Qabbani asked why naming what is the same matters, and Mrs Oueidat said because a category is a set of conditions and most of them are met, so a letter that says nine of the ten conditions are met and here is the tenth has done nine tenths of the reader\'s work. Mrs Rizk asked about two differences, and Mrs Khoury said then take them in two letters or accept that you are asking for an exception, because a letter with two is read as a general plea. Mr Shihabi asked about precedent, and that is the question he had never asked and it is in the second letter in one sentence, and they had one from 2016, and the secretary found it in two days and told him the category it went into, which was B. Mrs Tarabishi said so the precedent did the whole thing, and Mrs Khoury said the precedent did it and the question produced the precedent. Mrs Ajouz asked about the word unprecedented, and never use it about yourself. And Mr Attar said the thing he will take away is the two days, because he had been writing to that syndicate for five months about a category that did not exist, and one sentence produced a file from 2016 that had been there the whole time.']));
out.push(A('⚠ **The last line is the finding and the two numbers are the argument: five months, and two days.** **Five months of letters about a category that did not exist, and one sentence asking whether anybody had been registered like him produced a file from 2016 in two days** — **and the file had been there the whole time.** **Ask the room what the five months had been spent on, and the answer is a proposal nobody had the power to accept.**'));
out.push(S('Board clinic – typical mistakes'));
out.push(A('**1** ⚠ **A request for a new category** → **eighteen months and a committee paper.**   **2** _I do not fit any of them_ → **ten conditions for the reader to check unaided.**   **3** ⚠ _Unprecedented_ → **a boast, and wrong four times in five.**   **4** **Two differences in one letter** → **read as a general plea.**   **5** ⚠ **No count before the list** → **the reader cannot tell how much to read.**   **6** **A difference with no reason behind it** → **it reads as a defect in you rather than in the schedule.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 5 · Read'));
out.push(A('**1** ⚠ **He asks under which of the three existing categories the application falls, and he withdraws the request for a fourth made on 14 March.** **The withdrawal matters**: a file holding both requests holds two inconsistent applications, and a reader will answer the one that is easiest to refuse.'));
out.push(A('**2** ⚠ **Because it was established in 2014, after the list was last revised.** **A difference with a date behind it is an administrative fact about the schedule** — **and a difference with no reason given reads as a defect in the applicant, which is the same difference doing the opposite work.**'));
