out.push(h2('18.7  Review & Mediate: the applicant, the clerk, and the rule'));
out.push(S('Stage 1 · Get ready – Unit 18 quiz'));
out.push(A('**1** _…not on record, **which** you may attach to the form._ ⚠ **Delete _it_.**   **2** _…in order that no pupil **is registered** twice._   **3** _…grateful **to be told** to whom…_   **4** _…for the requirement **to be waived**._   **5** _…the file **would have gone** through in February._   **6** _…as the provisions are **presently** drawn._'));
out.push(S('Stage 2 · Listen and read'));
out.push(A('**b** ⚠ **That she could have told him in February.** **It is true: she could have, and she did not, because nobody had asked** — **and a letter that points it out has turned a two-line thank-you into a complaint about the one person who ended three months of difficulty in six days.**'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **This is the fifth mediation of Book 2 and the clearest case of nobody being at fault, and the room must be made to say so about each of the four accounts in turn.** **The applicant did not know the list existed.** **The clerk was never asked.** **The rule says nothing about declarations and was not written to.** **The list is eight years old and does exactly what everybody needed.** **The fault is in none of the four and lies in the gap between the third and the fourth** — **and a gap of that kind can only be closed by somebody with the power to publish, which is a section head.** ⚠ **Then the finding, and it must arrive last.** **The list has been in a drawer since 2017 because every applicant who got through it stopped writing on the day their own file went through.** **Six of the seven cycles in this unit are ways of getting your own file through a system; the seventh costs you something after you already have what you wanted** — **and that is the sentence Book 2 ends this half on.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 3 · Practise (sample – Pair A, the file and the unpublished list)'));
