out.push(A('**1** **INSTITUTIONAL**   **2** **BUREAUCRATIC**   **3** **ELIGIBILITY**   **4** **REGULATORY**   **5** **UNPRECEDENTED**   **6** **STATUTORY**   **7** **ANOMALOUS**   **8** **ACCOMMODATION**'));
out.push(A('⚠ **Part 3 is the part this class has lost most marks on across both books, and the losses are of two kinds: the wrong part of speech and the missing prefix.** **At 1 the gap needs an adjective to balance _personal_** — **and _institution_ is written by about a third of candidates.** **At 3 the gap follows _argue about_ and needs a noun; _eligible_ is written by candidates who have the right stem and have not read the preposition.** ⚠ **At 5 the whole item is the prefix.** **_Precedented_ is not a word and _unprecedented_ is what the sentence means** — **and this is the one item in the eight that cannot be solved by grammar, because it needs the sense of _almost nothing is_.** **At 8 accept only _accommodation_; _accommodating_ is a participle and the gap follows _this kind of_, which takes a noun.**'));
